<v Speaker 1>Who will indebt Allah with a beautiful debt?

131
00:16:24.590 --> 00:16:26.990
<v Speaker 1>So Allah is asking us for a loan.

132
00:16:28.350 --> 00:16:33.470
<v Speaker 1>Who will indebt Allah with a beautiful debt?

133
00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:35.310
<v Speaker 1>Why is Allah asking us for a loan?

134
00:16:39.150 --> 00:16:46.750
<v Speaker 1>So that Allah multiplies its rewards many many times over and returns it back to his life.

135
00:16:49.710 --> 00:16:56.990
<v Speaker 1>So in this verse, Allah is actually asking His slaves, Who among you will give me a loan?

136
00:16:57.310 --> 00:16:57.710
<v Speaker 1>Right?

137
00:16:57.710 --> 00:17:09.950
<v Speaker 1>Who among you will indebt me with His willing submission of 'ubu diyya, so that I can multiply its rewards many many times over and pay it back to you.

138
00:17:10.830 --> 00:17:13.950
<v Speaker 1>For He has the most noble rewards.

139
00:17:15.310 --> 00:17:15.990
<v Speaker 1>Subhanallah.

140
00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:21.790
<v Speaker 1>Even on that day of hisaab, this Malik is full of love and mercy.

141
00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:30.510
<v Speaker 1>So that is what Malik-i-Aumiddin linguistically means.

142
00:17:31.310 --> 00:17:36.750
<v Speaker 1>The king or the owner of the time period when the debt of submission falls due.

143
