147
00:18:14.910 --> 00:18:22.190
<v Speaker 1>Now this can be based on an injustice that happened to them personally or injustices that happens to another.

148
00:18:23.390 --> 00:18:29.870
<v Speaker 1>And their argument is that if there is a God that is so loving and caring, then how come He let all of this happen?

149
00:18:32.830 --> 00:18:44.390
<v Speaker 1>Now, what's interesting about that, especially to us as a Muslim, is that nowhere in the Quran, Allah claims or promises to give us a good life in this world.

150
00:18:45.710 --> 00:18:46.350
<v Speaker 1>Nowhere.

151
00:18:47.790 --> 00:18:53.310
<v Speaker 1>In fact, what He promises every human being is quite the opposite.

152
00:18:54.350 --> 00:19:04.830
<v Speaker 1>He says, in Surat-ul-Baqarah, He says, wala nabluwannakum bishayim minal khawfi wal jewari wa naqsim minal amwali wal anfusi wa thamaraat.

153
00:19:06.990 --> 00:19:12.590
<v Speaker 1>And no doubt about it, indeed, surely we shall test you with fear.

154
00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:21.790
<v Speaker 1>with hunger, with loss of wealth, with loss of life, children, with loss of crops.

155
00:19:23.630 --> 00:19:30.350
<v Speaker 1>But then he says, O Bashir Sabireen and for the patient ones there are glad tidings.

156
